<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- THE DISCOVERY MEASUREMENT HARNESS. Not part of the product. It answers one question
       with numbers instead of a guess: what automatic Self-Membership discovery costs, so a
       production processing budget can be recommended and approved. Decision 0102 refuses to
       invent a universal threshold and the unmeasured 50-pair proposal was withdrawn; measuring
       is what replaces it.

       A SEPARATE EXECUTABLE ON PURPOSE. Measurement is not a test: a suite asserts correctness
       and must stay fast and deterministic, while this runs for minutes and reports figures
       nobody can assert in advance. Folding it into the tests would let an execution time be
       mistaken for a passing check, which docs/next/README.md gate 1 exists to prevent.

       THE LEGACY MODE CONTACTS NOTHING AND WRITES NOTHING INTO THE REPOSITORY. Every bundle it judges it
       wrote itself, beneath the system temporary directory, and each is deleted as soon as its
       shape is measured. Sealed Evidence, next/artifacts and the laboratory directory are never
       opened for writing.

       The explicitly selected requester mode instead retains every input and result in a new
       caller-supplied directory. Existing captures are copied and hash-checked, never judged in
       place. This is the approved P-242 offline measurement, not production activation.

       DELETE THIS PROJECT once a discovery budget is measured, approved and recorded. That record
       was to go in docs/layers/judgement/the-judgement-store.md, which was deleted on 2026-09-12
       with the other layer documents; an approved budget is an owner decision, so it now belongs in
       docs/WHAT-THE-PRODUCT-IS.md. The open question is P-152. Kept past that point this becomes a
       second account of how judging performs, free to drift from the product it describes. -->

  <!-- RESP-01 also uses this executable for explicitly selected current-format offline controls.
       That mode retains new outputs and refuses reuse; it runs the current host catalogue and
       policy, not the legacy discovery sweep. Producer/readback controls are not a complete UI
       baseline or enterprise acceptance. Keep the historical modes and their evidence intact. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>SecureAD.Measure</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SecureAD.Measure</AssemblyName>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <!-- Matched to the referenced projects, which are x64 so SQLite native loading resolves. -->
    <PlatformTarget>x64</PlatformTarget>
    <RuntimeIdentifier>win-x64</RuntimeIdentifier>
    <SelfContained>false</SelfContained>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SecureAD.Next.Tests" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SecureAD.Kernel\SecureAD.Kernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SecureAD.Evidence\SecureAD.Evidence.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SecureAD.Derivation\SecureAD.Derivation.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SecureAD.Judgement\SecureAD.Judgement.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
